# 🐳 Phase 3 — Docker

**Goal:** a small, non-root image that builds without needing Redis at build time.

```bash
git checkout develop && git checkout -b feature/phase3-docker
cd app/src
```

### Step 3.1 — Replace `app/src/Dockerfile`
```dockerfile
# ---------- Stage 1: production dependencies ----------
FROM node:20-alpine AS deps
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --omit=dev

# ---------- Stage 2: runtime ----------
FROM node:20-alpine AS runtime
WORKDIR /app
RUN apk add --no-cache dumb-init && \
    addgroup -g 1001 -S nodejs && \
    adduser -S nodejs -u 1001 && \
    mkdir -p /app/logs && chown -R nodejs:nodejs /app
COPY --from=deps --chown=nodejs:nodejs /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --chown=nodejs:nodejs . .
USER nodejs
EXPOSE 3000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=10s --retries=3 \
  CMD node -e "require('http').get('http://localhost:3000/health',r=>process.exit([200,503].includes(r.statusCode)?0:1)).on('error',()=>process.exit(1))"
ENTRYPOINT ["dumb-init", "--"]
CMD ["node", "src/server.js"]
```
> 🧠 **Why:** tests now run in CI (Phase 7), not inside the image. Final image is Alpine, non-root (UID 1001), with `dumb-init` for clean `SIGTERM` handling.

